  "extraction": "Published HTML examples are extracted from paired pre/code.language-markdown and pre/code.language-html nodes, with HTMLParser entity decoding and space marker spans converted to literal spaces. Markdown is never reverse-derived from expected HTML. Pinned spec_tests.py convention maps U+2192 to a tab on both Markdown and expected HTML in the source corpora. Repository spec parsing follows pinned test/spec_tests.py: every example including disabled tags is retained, literal arrow glyphs become tabs in Markdown and HTML, intentional CR characters are preserved, and original source line ranges are recorded. The full published page contributes all paired examples, including the empty HTML expectations for IDs 176 and 188, while repository corpora remain distinct and corpus-qualified.",
